# Full-Screen Focus Mode

The goal is to transition the Focus page from its current "windowed" design (a centered card with a border) to a full-screen, immersive experience. This will make the focus environment feel more atmospheric and less constrained.

## Proposed Changes

### Focus Page

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/focus/page.tsx)

- **Remove the centered card container**: Modify the container div (around line 835) that currently has `max-w-5xl`, `border`, and `glass-card` classes.
- **Expand layout to full viewport**:
    - Make the main content area occupy the full width and height below the header.
    - Implement a three-column grid for Large Mode (Spotify Enabled):
        - Left: Spotify Player (immersive/minimal).
        - Center: Large Clock and Timer Controls.
        - Right: Task List.
- **Background Layer refinement**: Ensure the background presets (Animated, Gradient, Image) remain as the bottom layer and cover the entire viewport without gaps.
- **Overlay adjustment**: Keep the dark overlay (`bg-black/50`) but ensure it covers the whole screen to maintain readability of white text/icons over diverse backgrounds.
- **Responsiveness**: Ensure the layout folds gracefully on smaller screens, potentially moving the task list to the bottom or a toggleable side panel.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- **Visual Audit**: I will use the browser tool to navigate to `/focus` and verify:
    - The "windowed" border is gone.
    - The layout spans the full width of the screen.
    - All background presets (Matrix, Starfield, etc.) scale correctly to the full screen.
- **Functional Check**:
    - Verify Spotify player still works and is positioned well.
    - Verify timer controls (Start/Pause/Reset) are functional and centered.
    - Verify task list is accessible and usable.
    - Test responsive behavior by resizing the browser window.
